{"module_id":25,"type":"fill_command","difficulty":"easy","prompt":"Write the command to list all token privileges for the current Windows user, including privilege state:","options":None,"answer":"whoami /priv","explanation":"whoami /priv shows all token privileges and whether each is Enabled or Disabled. SeImpersonatePrivilege or SeAssignPrimaryTokenPrivilege enables Potato attacks for SYSTEM access. SeBackupPrivilege allows reading any file. SeDebugPrivilege enables process injection.","validation_regex":"whoami /priv","hints":["This is the first command to run on Windows targets","Look for SeImpersonatePrivilege"]},
{"module_id":25,"type":"fill_command","difficulty":"medium","prompt":"Write the wmic command to find all Windows services with auto-start and unquoted executable paths (potential unquoted service path vulnerability):","options":None,"answer":"wmic service get name,displayname,pathname,startmode | findstr /i \"auto\" | findstr /i /v \"c:\\windows\"","explanation":"Unquoted paths with spaces are vulnerable when a directory in the path is writable. Windows tries to execute each word as an executable (C:\\Program.exe, then C:\\Program Files\\App.exe). Place evil.exe at the first writable location in the path.","validation_regex":"wmic service get.*pathname.*startmode","hints":["Look for paths with spaces that are not in quotes","Services that auto-start run as the configured user (often SYSTEM)"]},
{"module_id":25,"type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":"medium","prompt":"SeImpersonatePrivilege is enabled in whoami /priv. Which tool gives the fastest path to SYSTEM on a modern Windows 10/11 or Server 2019/2022 target?","options":["JuicyPotato","RottenPotato","GodPotato","PrintSpoofer (Server 2016-2019 only)"],"answer":"GodPotato","explanation":"GodPotato works on Windows Server 2012 through 2022 and Windows 8 through 11 — the broadest compatibility for modern targets. JuicyPotato requires a specific CLSID and doesn't work on Server 2019+. PrintSpoofer works on Server 2016 and 2019 but not 2022.","validation_regex":None,"hints":["Which Potato variant has the broadest Windows version support?","Think about Windows 10/11 and Server 2019/2022 compatibility"]},
